prs.body:
Since https://github.com/laravel/framework/pull/58241 enums are now available for the session keys this PR aligns it for the cache too.

I've done it this way via the Repository as we don't need to edit each store - and then update each store test - and its available on the Cache facade too.

I've added a test to cover the methods just to be sure,  the Cache facade will be updated if this is accepted / merged via the workflow.

We could edit the contract in 13.x and the other implementations perhaps. 

Just wanted to try this as a simpler way to get enums in, otherwise it'll have to be a full fat PR


This just means we can do:

```php

// Before 
Session::put(AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE, 'x'); // Session allows enums.
$result = Graphs::where('x', AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE)->first(); // we can already do it on the query builder.. :)
Cache::put(AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE->value, $result); // NO ENUM SUPPORT?


// After 
Session::put(AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE, 'x');
$result = Graphs::where('x', AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE)->first();
Cache::put(AnalyticalGraph::PROFILE, $result);
```

